Chisel2Lean4

This project derives from Chicala:
https://github.com/iscas-tis/chicala

The upstream baseline is commit:
c8bab84b24c448c611b8bf2a87c7e9c26014b081

The original Apache License, Version 2.0 is retained in LICENSE.
The upstream README is retained in docs/upstream/README.md.

This distribution includes additions and modifications for the parameterized
Lean 4 intermediate representation, backend, runtime, source diagnostics,
command-line execution, and independent RTL differential validation.

The XiangShan RightShiftModule validation fixture is derived from
OpenXiangShan/XiangShan and retains its original Mulan PSL v2 license and
copyright notices. See verification/xiangshan/right-shift/SOURCE.json and
verification/xiangshan/right-shift/upstream/LICENSE for provenance and terms.

XiangShan v2.1 FIRRTL validation
Derived FIRRTL circuits in verification/xiangshan/firrtl originate from
OpenXiangShan/XiangShan commit f0d8a1cf543c113433ff98140b6d77055d930deb.
Original modules and parameter framework are elaborated without logic changes.
Upstream Mulan PSL v2 license is retained alongside the artifacts.
The classic frontend uses the Apache-2.0 licensed official Scala FIRRTL 1.5.6
library. GSIM is a design reference, not a copied implementation or dependency.

The real CDE implementation in vendor/cde is copied without modification from
chipsalliance/cde commit 52768c97a27b254c0cc0ac9401feb55b29e18c28. Its original
Apache-2.0 license and source checksum are retained in vendor/cde.
Full XiangShan configuration integration uses immutable source dependencies
listed in verification/xiangshan/config-dependencies.json. Fetched dependency
sources and their original licenses remain in the project-local cache.

The modern Chisel 7.3 elaboration validation also uses the unchanged Nanhu
L2TlbPrefetch and AluDataModule under the same immutable dependency lock.
Modern FIRRTL is parsed and normalized by the Apache-2.0 with LLVM-exception
licensed CIRCT firtool 1.135.0; its generic MLIR SSA output is imported by a
new reader. No CIRCT source implementation is copied into this project.

The fixed-RTL frontend uses upstream Yosys 0.70 FunctionalIR and its existing
SMT-LIB serializer, through the project-local YoWASP distribution. The bundled
slang/sv-elab frontend performs SystemVerilog elaboration. Wheel SHA256 hashes
are fixed in scripts/bootstrap_yosys.py; upstream and dependency licenses remain
in the extracted wheel metadata. The Python reader and Lean exporter are new
code; no Yosys, slang, sv-elab or Sparkle source implementation is vendored.
